00:55:37.010 --> 00:55:44.270
Yes, senor. Where's Barbecue?

00:55:47.920 --> 00:55:51.260
I'll wait. Giselle, drink?

00:55:52.140 --> 00:55:52.440
Oh, thanks.

00:55:53.720 --> 00:55:54.740
I'll have a drink, senor.

00:55:55.660 --> 00:55:56.780
Is it all right?

00:55:57.200 --> 00:55:58.360
Is it all right, Gingalit?

00:55:58.650 --> 00:55:59.510
Sure, give her a drink.

00:56:01.610 --> 00:56:12.130
Bonata, she's a big girl. Give her a drink.

00:56:13.130 --> 00:56:14.250
You heard what he said, Mosso.

00:56:14.560 --> 00:56:15.220
Give me scotch.

00:56:34.160 --> 00:56:39.740
You're nice, gringolito. I want to drink with you.

00:56:42.950 --> 00:56:43.430
I don't drink.

00:56:45.400 --> 00:56:46.320
Is that because you're good?

00:56:48.720 --> 00:56:49.000
Particularly.

00:56:50.180 --> 00:56:56.830
You are good. A good little angler with pretty brown eyes and lots of American dollars.

00:56:57.750 --> 00:56:58.410
Where's Barthek?

00:56:59.700 --> 00:56:59.960
Didn't you?

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:03.760
Do you hear the motto? He's not in. Dance with me.

00:57:03.880 --> 00:57:05.000
What is he?

00:57:06.200 --> 00:57:10.340
Dance with me. If you dance with me, I'll tell you.

00:57:12.940 --> 00:57:13.320
Oh, yeah.

00:57:20.340 --> 00:57:22.320
With Bobic in his office.

00:58:00.350 --> 00:58:07.700
So few women in Tier 1, you must look for one in my office.

00:58:13.900 --> 00:58:14.360
Get out.

00:58:15.780 --> 00:58:17.480
There's a particular kind of a woman, Bartik.

00:58:17.740 --> 00:58:18.800
What kind of woman is that?

00:58:19.660 --> 00:58:21.050
The kind that Al Wolfe would at you.

00:58:21.390 --> 00:58:22.350
The kind that needed help.

00:58:22.610 --> 00:58:23.790
Like Lombard needed help.

00:58:25.270 --> 00:58:26.350
He doesn't need it anymore.

00:58:31.180 --> 00:58:36.900
What about 14 Cali Rosarito del Flores Tijuana?

00:58:37.100 --> 00:58:45.970
About that woman, Baric.

00:58:47.920 --> 00:58:49.820
I've known about you and Al Wolf for a long time,

00:58:49.960 --> 00:58:51.520
playing your high-class wetback game.

00:58:52.540 --> 00:58:54.640
A lot of people could use a passport away out of the country,

00:58:54.780 --> 00:58:59.450
but it paid.

00:59:00.250 --> 00:59:02.150
At Bart Wolf, an airport in your club?

00:59:03.920 --> 00:59:04.280
Crazy.

00:59:04.940 --> 00:59:06.140
I haven't got much time.

00:59:06.610 --> 00:59:07.250
Where's the woman?

00:59:09.360 --> 00:59:09.800
Police?

00:59:17.360 --> 00:59:17.980
Take your tour.

00:59:25.760 --> 00:59:27.710
First, I phone call.

00:59:32.880 --> 00:59:33.900
You're not very bright, Bobby.

00:59:35.820 --> 00:59:36.400
Very well.

00:59:37.740 --> 00:59:38.540
She's here, safe.

00:59:39.870 --> 00:59:42.110
Husband arranged for two Argentine passports.

00:59:42.960 --> 00:59:44.620
After the border of Vianzco, I took her in.

00:59:44.940 --> 00:59:45.780
You still have the passports?

00:59:46.980 --> 00:59:47.220
Yes.

00:59:48.620 --> 00:59:48.860
Beautiful.

00:59:49.620 --> 00:59:50.280
And the way out of Mexico?

00:59:50.520 --> 00:59:51.340
Also beautiful.

00:59:52.860 --> 00:59:53.280
Cost money.

00:59:53.530 --> 00:59:53.810
How much?

00:59:55.300 --> 00:59:56.020
A thousand dollars.

00:59:56.680 --> 00:59:57.440
But it is foolproof.

00:59:58.640 --> 00:59:59.980
I'd send my own mother that way.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:03.520
You probably have. I'll be using those passports.

01:00:05.030 --> 01:00:06.740
You? For yourself?

01:00:07.020 --> 01:00:07.820
I want them tomorrow night.

01:00:09.520 --> 01:00:09.700
Morning?

01:00:10.350 --> 01:00:12.490
Half tomorrow night. Half when you get us into Buenos Aires.

01:00:13.160 --> 01:00:16.190
Don't argue, Father. I'm not in the mood. Take me to work.

01:00:31.690 --> 01:00:32.150
Hello, Linda.

01:00:34.140 --> 01:00:34.540
Charlie.

01:01:00.090 --> 01:01:03.890
wanted to go with Paul. Charlie threatened

01:01:03.890 --> 01:01:07.160
to tell the police. Money gave

01:01:07.160 --> 01:01:09.620
him a feeling of power. Dreams

01:01:09.620 --> 01:01:16.800
of a new life. Me and me.

01:01:25.040 --> 01:01:26.260
Sure the money will be out of me tomorrow.

01:01:27.660 --> 01:01:28.740
Hours will be halfway to origin.

01:01:31.280 --> 01:01:31.760
We'll be together.

01:01:32.390 --> 01:01:35.420
Two of us.

01:01:43.520 --> 01:01:45.890
Charlie, I was just going to look for you.

01:01:47.120 --> 01:01:47.680
Oh, what's up?

01:01:48.240 --> 01:01:50.910
We just got a call from Cabot, Leighton Prince.

01:01:51.600 --> 01:01:53.080
We've got an ID on Sloan.

01:01:54.200 --> 01:01:55.200
Old Doc Sloan.

01:01:55.720 --> 01:01:57.180
His real name was Paul Bruckner.

01:01:57.780 --> 01:01:58.820
Lived in San Francisco.

01:01:59.660 --> 01:01:59.980
Married...

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:01.340
to a Mexican girl named Linda.

01:02:02.150 --> 01:02:03.190
He was legitimate, too,

01:02:03.750 --> 01:02:04.410
until he was kicked out

01:02:04.410 --> 01:02:05.110
from malpractice.

01:02:06.330 --> 01:02:07.310
You're creeping up on him.

01:02:07.900 --> 01:02:09.340
Once you've got a man's right name,

01:02:09.360 --> 01:02:11.020
he quits being a shadow.

01:02:12.300 --> 01:02:13.200
What's the next step?

01:02:13.890 --> 01:02:15.170
We dig into Bruckner's life

01:02:15.170 --> 01:02:15.970
in San Francisco.

01:02:16.710 --> 01:02:17.870
What tonsils he took out,

01:02:18.380 --> 01:02:19.480
what babies he delivered,

01:02:20.400 --> 01:02:21.480
how he lost his license.

01:02:25.080 --> 01:02:25.920
Are you all scotting, Joe?

01:02:26.140 --> 01:02:27.060
Me? Oh, thanks.

01:02:27.240 --> 01:02:28.220
I'm still excited enough.

01:02:29.130 --> 01:02:29.970
Besides, I had to...

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:40.520
drink you a beer too last night. Last night? I went right to my room. So I better get going. I've

01:02:40.520 --> 01:02:44.860
got to meet Ruth at the border. What does she do? I'll go with you. That's all right,

01:02:44.900 --> 01:02:50.300
John. Thanks. Sure you can, but I don't want to miss seeing Ruth's face when she finally gets to

01:02:50.300 --> 01:02:50.660
Mexico.

01:03:14.200 --> 01:03:21.330
Wait a minute. Looks like you're going away for ten years.

01:03:21.840 --> 01:03:23.360
Yes, it looks like it, doesn't it?

01:03:51.280 --> 01:03:52.040
Shall we unpack now?

01:03:53.260 --> 01:03:54.840
Fine. Why don't we be left at her dinner?

01:03:56.310 --> 01:03:58.450
Whenever you say, Charlie, I'm tired.

01:03:59.650 --> 01:03:59.970
Very tired.

01:04:02.010 --> 01:04:03.670
Why don't you take a nap for an hour or so?

01:04:04.120 --> 01:04:04.920
Well, what'll you be doing?

01:04:08.710 --> 01:04:10.030
Thought I'd go over these annual reports.

01:04:10.250 --> 01:04:10.570
Why?

01:04:14.070 --> 01:04:15.670
Did you deserve that job for Mexico City?

01:04:19.910 --> 01:04:20.510
Here's my mind.

01:04:24.210 --> 01:04:25.510
I think I'll do it now.

01:04:26.720 --> 01:04:29.160
I was going to surprise you to take along your fishing gear.

01:04:30.510 --> 01:04:34.280
Put it in there, so I had a key made, and I opened the case.

01:04:39.860 --> 01:04:45.580
It would be a surprise, a joke, something to laugh about.

01:04:59.050 --> 01:04:59.710
What did you do with the money?

01:05:02.360 --> 01:05:04.300
I mail it to Mr. Hendricks, no return address.

01:05:07.650 --> 01:05:09.350
Crazy fool, you know what you've done, do you?

01:05:14.080 --> 01:05:14.980
To do it, why?

01:05:15.840 --> 01:05:16.100
Why?

01:05:17.990 --> 01:05:18.650
What does it matter?

01:05:18.770 --> 01:05:20.430
I killed a man to protect that money.

01:05:24.170 --> 01:05:25.350
Kill me, won't you, Charlie?

01:05:26.110 --> 01:05:29.950
You want to?

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:35.020
from me. A few hours. Just a few

01:05:35.020 --> 01:05:41.820
hours. I gave you my whole life. What's

01:05:41.820 --> 01:05:53.190
the few hours? Don't turn away

01:05:53.190 --> 01:05:56.040
from me. Let me catch you. Let me talk to you.

01:06:00.280 --> 01:06:02.380
say. There's so much to say.

01:06:03.910 --> 01:06:06.730
Please, at least tell me what we were going to do.

01:06:11.200 --> 01:06:15.630
I don't do anything. He's going to leave you.

01:06:19.960 --> 01:06:27.470
He loved you, Charlie. But enough. He was.

01:06:30.220 --> 01:06:31.120
What if did I fail you?

01:06:33.980 --> 01:06:34.420
I didn't fail.

01:06:35.080 --> 01:06:35.840
People change.

01:06:41.440 --> 01:06:42.660
That's so much, Charlie.

01:06:43.960 --> 01:06:44.260
Why?

01:06:44.540 --> 01:06:44.700
Why?

01:06:45.100 --> 01:06:50.990
It becomes a prisoner job, a trap.

01:06:53.580 --> 01:06:54.440
What did you want?

01:06:55.720 --> 01:06:58.720
A new kind of life, the kind that $200,000 could have bought me.

01:07:02.720 --> 01:07:03.040
Alone?

01:07:07.350 --> 01:07:07.670
Alone.

01:07:11.670 --> 01:07:12.310
Have that now.

01:07:15.860 --> 01:07:16.300
No, you think.

01:07:19.140 --> 01:07:24.390
Charlie, if you went to them, if you said I did it, I'm sorry you're getting the money back.

01:07:26.240 --> 01:07:27.510
Charlie, I'd wait.

01:07:27.510 --> 01:07:28.290
I'd have the strength.

01:07:28.290 --> 01:07:29.070
I'd have the patience.

01:07:29.210 --> 01:07:29.970
I'd wait no matter how.

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:34.890
long. There isn't time enough in all eternity, Ruth. I killed a man. You couldn't wait for me.

01:07:49.780 --> 01:07:50.760
But you weren't alone.

01:08:17.880 --> 01:08:20.030
Wait a minute, the more on Bruckner.

01:08:21.860 --> 01:08:21.960
What?

01:08:22.390 --> 01:08:23.810
Lieutenant Castro checked it for me.

01:08:24.380 --> 01:08:25.360
A hunch, but he paid off.

01:08:26.370 --> 01:08:29.690
Bruckner was married here in Tijuana seven years ago to a singer in a club named...

01:08:30.410 --> 01:08:31.930
Linda Alvarez.

01:08:32.510 --> 01:08:33.070
Where was that club?

01:08:33.580 --> 01:08:35.260
In Agua Caliente, but they went out of business.

01:08:36.120 --> 01:08:37.540
Did she sing anyplace else?

01:08:38.280 --> 01:08:38.600
Perhaps.

01:08:38.960 --> 01:08:40.060
It won't take long to find out.

01:08:40.560 --> 01:08:41.680
There are a few secrets in Tijuana.

01:08:43.340 --> 01:08:43.700
I've got to go.

01:08:43.760 --> 01:08:44.700
I've got to get some things for Ruth.

01:08:44.920 --> 01:08:46.500
No, no.

01:08:46.790 --> 01:08:47.950
Not until you have a drink with me.

01:08:48.910 --> 01:08:50.310
Or did you have too much to drink last night?

01:08:51.660 --> 01:08:54.140
One of my men saw the car park right next to Bobbix last night.

01:08:55.690 --> 01:08:57.850
Police cars attract an awful lot of attention in that district.

01:09:00.640 --> 01:09:02.780
I stopped for a drink on my way back from the airport.

01:09:04.100 --> 01:09:05.460
It wasn't the drink you stopped for.

01:09:05.680 --> 01:09:07.440
You probably heard about the dancer they have there.

01:09:08.290 --> 01:09:09.090
She's pretty nice, huh?

01:09:09.760 --> 01:09:11.190
Yeah, yeah, she's right.

01:09:14.800 --> 01:09:15.180
I'll get around.

01:09:15.890 --> 01:09:16.250
See you later.

01:09:17.240 --> 01:09:18.280
Very impatient man.

01:09:20.490 --> 01:09:22.030
Bob, it's just hardly the place for a tourist.

01:09:22.560 --> 01:09:24.800
Or is your friend trying to combine business with pleasure?

01:09:27.760 --> 01:09:27.980
Maybe.

01:09:38.380 --> 01:09:38.800
Who is it?

01:09:39.670 --> 01:09:40.350
It's Joe Ruth.

01:09:40.970 --> 01:09:41.470
Can I come in?

01:09:41.960 --> 01:09:42.740
Oh, wait a minute.

01:09:52.930 --> 01:09:53.170
Come in.

01:10:10.430 --> 01:10:10.890
Anything wrong?

01:10:11.010 --> 01:10:14.870
Of course not.

01:10:14.990 --> 01:10:15.230
Why?

01:10:15.510 --> 01:10:20.980
I don't know.

01:10:21.120 --> 01:10:22.940
You and Charlie, you both seem a bit edgy.

01:10:23.580 --> 01:10:24.400
Sure everything's all right.

01:10:24.460 --> 01:10:26.140
I just told you, everything is fine.

01:10:28.080 --> 01:10:28.780
Why shouldn't it be?

01:10:37.130 --> 01:10:40.080
Ruth, I've known you a long time.

01:10:45.480 --> 01:10:46.080
What do you mean?

01:10:46.180 --> 01:10:47.020
Is Charlie in any trouble?

01:10:49.490 --> 01:10:50.590
Don't you stop being a cop.

01:10:50.690 --> 01:10:51.710
You make a case out of everything.

01:10:51.910 --> 01:10:53.090
Ruth, you're making one out of this.

01:10:53.210 --> 01:10:54.010
Well, there's no trouble.

01:10:54.250 --> 01:10:56.540
There's a few words between husband and wife.

01:11:01.980 --> 01:11:03.300
Sometimes Charlie flies off.

01:11:05.380 --> 01:11:06.640
It's that little argument, that's all.

01:11:07.800 --> 01:11:10.330
How can anybody argue with you?

01:11:11.240 --> 01:11:12.460
Or maybe I'm just prejudiced.

01:11:14.690 --> 01:11:15.530
Who knows better than you?

01:11:15.750 --> 01:11:17.090
Charlie's been under a lot of strain.

01:11:17.190 --> 01:11:18.550
Sure, every case is an ulcer.

01:11:20.260 --> 01:11:23.630
And this one, the way our Charlie's been riding himself.

01:11:25.720 --> 01:11:26.080
Maybe.

01:11:27.750 --> 01:11:28.610
Interfered with his holiday.

01:11:28.750 --> 01:11:29.710
He promised it to himself.

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:44.600
me. A real fiesta. The way a kid looks forward to a birthday party. Just overworked. He's

01:11:44.600 --> 01:11:57.540
been edgy for months. Ever since Hendricks sent him up to San Francisco. Well, I hadn't

01:11:57.540 --> 01:11:59.080
read them. I expected to on the plane.

01:12:00.600 --> 01:12:02.040
It's a long trip to Mexico City.

01:12:07.290 --> 01:12:18.580
Yeah, long trip. All of six hours. Enough reading for a year.

01:12:30.640 --> 01:12:34.060
Operator, I want to speak to Mr. Sam Hendricks,

01:12:35.470 --> 01:12:43.680
Victoria 9-4-9-0-1, Burbank, California.

01:12:47.780 --> 01:12:48.040
Right away?

01:12:55.400 --> 01:12:57.200
Oh, Hendricks, Armstrong.

01:12:58.870 --> 01:12:59.510
Yeah, from Tier 1.

01:13:01.080 --> 01:13:01.940
Oh, fine, fine.

01:13:03.090 --> 01:13:07.230
Look, Hendricks, Charlie was on a case several months ago up in San Francisco.

01:13:08.500 --> 01:13:09.540
Can you give me any dope on it?

01:13:11.610 --> 01:13:12.770
I'll explain later.

01:13:15.280 --> 01:13:15.800
Yes, I'll wait.

01:13:17.490 --> 01:13:19.070
You know, people on the plane are choosy.

01:13:19.210 --> 01:13:22.030
They like to read things that are bright,

01:13:23.380 --> 01:13:25.930
take their mind off the possibility of a crash.

01:13:27.780 --> 01:13:28.540
I'll repeat that.

01:13:30.440 --> 01:13:31.820
A phony accident claim.

01:13:33.030 --> 01:13:33.910
Eight months ago, huh?

01:13:36.200 --> 01:13:36.300
Yeah.

01:13:39.350 --> 01:13:49.900
Dr. Paul Bruckner, thank you.

01:13:54.970 --> 01:13:57.960
Take that line, don't crash.

01:14:02.010 --> 01:14:02.770
I'm sorry, Ruth.

01:14:15.960 --> 01:14:16.440
No plan.

01:14:16.640 --> 01:14:18.460
I changed my mind.

01:14:19.110 --> 01:14:20.390
I don't want to go to Buenos Aires direct.

01:14:20.700 --> 01:14:21.920
I want to go to Waka Waka Waka by boat.

01:14:23.040 --> 01:14:24.560
I'll pay you more for the passports.

01:14:25.900 --> 01:14:26.520
How much more?

01:14:28.440 --> 01:14:28.760
A thousand.

01:14:30.060 --> 01:14:37.380
Why not? $25,000. Payable now. You get everything. Passports, bus certificates, everything.

01:14:38.770 --> 01:14:39.730
What about Passage South?

01:14:40.600 --> 01:14:44.110
Si Alfredo Rodriguez. Casa del Norte, Rosarito Beach.

01:14:45.080 --> 01:14:48.570
You tell him Bubbik sent him a fisherman, he will understand.

01:14:49.380 --> 01:14:50.000
What will he charge?

01:14:51.040 --> 01:14:59.660
What does it matter? A few hundred dollars, maybe five, six hundred. Who knows? Cheap money.

01:15:01.340 --> 01:15:02.500
If you've got the passports.

01:15:04.840 --> 01:15:06.980
Tell you, you tell me.

01:15:08.460 --> 01:15:08.780
Children.

01:15:26.400 --> 01:15:27.060
Leave the money public.

01:15:41.390 --> 01:15:41.810
Come on.

01:16:17.920 --> 01:16:26.550
Make it the other side of the street.

01:16:26.780 --> 01:16:28.640
Give it to the manzana and close the door.

01:16:28.960 --> 01:16:29.980
And call the manager that...

01:16:30.412 --> 01:16:32.412
Thank you very much.

01:18:01.820 --> 01:18:03.750
Cover that door and you cover the back door.

01:19:51.660 --> 01:19:52.460
timetable either.
